    {"id": 5, "claim": "Statement I ('post(u) < post(v)') is false. In a tree, if u is an ancestor of v, the postorder traversal visits v (and its subtree) before u. Thus, post(v) < post(u).", "evidence": "Postorder traversal definition: children are visited before parents. If u is an ancestor of v, v is in u's subtree, so v is finished before u.", "weight": 1.0, "depends_on": [2]},
